; DECLARATION PRELUDE — consumed via `babylon_bsl::scenario::
; load_scenario_with_prelude` (Train B item 4, issue #591, D157 —
; docs/reference/bsl-language.rst §2.13). NOT a scenario: no
; `(scenario <qname> ...)` wrapper, and only the four declaration top-forms
; are legal here (`defenum` / `defvocabulary` / `defconst` / `deffield`) —
; a prelude declares, it never seeds a graph.
;
; The WorldView mint (ADR206), factored out of the mint scenario
; (worldview-foundation.bscn) so a consuming scenario can resolve
; `WorldView`-typed fields WITHOUT re-declaring the type itself. A scenario
; MAY still re-declare it verbatim (`EnumRegistry::declare`'s identical-
; recognition arm resolves to the SAME id, this train); a scenario that
; declares it differently still refuses, exactly as any other conflicting
; `defenum` does.
;
; Member order is RULED content (design doc §4.1, Director-approved
; 2026-08-14): REVOLUTIONARY / LIBERAL / FASCIST. Declaration order IS the
; storage ordinal (ADR195), so the ruled order makes REVOLUTIONARY=0,
; LIBERAL=1, FASCIST=2 — byte-identical to worldview-foundation.bscn's own
; declaration.
(defenum WorldView (REVOLUTIONARY LIBERAL FASCIST))
